---
---
<section id="guide" class="py-16 md:py-24 lg:py-32 border-t border-hairline bg-canvas relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6 relative z-10">
    
    <!-- Short Intro -->
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-20 md:mb-24">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft text-[10px] font-mono text-mute mb-6 select-none">
        <span class="flex h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-500/60 dark:bg-indigo-400/80"></span>
        SEO & Sizing Guide
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-6 text-balance leading-tight">
        Instagram No Crop Tool: Fit & Resize Photos Without Cropping
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-2xl text-pretty font-normal">
        Posting high-quality images on social media often comes with the frustrating limitation of standard cropping. Our free, browser-based <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Instagram No Crop Tool</strong> is designed for creators, brands, and casual users alike. It serves as a comprehensive <strong class="text-ink font-medium">no crop instagram post maker</strong> and a versatile <strong class="text-ink font-medium">social media aspect ratio converter</strong>, allowing you to <strong class="text-ink font-medium">resize photo for instagram without cropping</strong> any critical detail of your shot.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Why Instagram Crops Photos -->
    <div class="border-t border-hairline py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 md:gap-12 items-start">
        <div class="md:col-span-5">
          <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink text-pretty leading-snug">
            Why do social platforms crop your photos automatically?
          </h3>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-7">
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty">
            Instagram supports several specific aspect ratios, such as 1:1 square, 4:5 portrait, and 16:9 landscape, while Stories and Reels use a vertical 9:16 ratio. When you upload a photo that does not match these dimensions, the platform forces you to crop it. 
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty mt-4">
            By using our <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram image resizer online</strong>, you can convert any photo format instantly. It functions as an <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram full size photo tool</strong> that fits the entire image within the required social media dimensions by padding the edges instead of cropping the subject. Whether you need an <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram landscape photo fit tool</strong> or an <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram portrait resize tool</strong>, this generator adapts to your unique image styling needs in a matter of seconds.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Supported Aspect Ratios -->
    <div class="border-t border-hairline py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4 leading-tight">
          Supported Aspect Ratios
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty max-w-2xl">
          Easily switch between different formats with our one-click presets. The tool acts as a <strong class="text-ink font-medium">social media aspect ratio converter</strong> supporting the exact resolutions recommended by top platforms:
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        
        <!-- Ratio Card 1: 1:1 -->
        <div class="glass-card glass-card-hover rounded-xl p-5 border border-hairline flex flex-col justify-between transition-all duration-200">
          <div>
            <div class="h-24 w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] bg-[radial-gradient(var(--grid-dot)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:8px_8px]"></div>
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded border border-hairline-strong/60 bg-ink/[0.03] dark:bg-white/[0.03] flex items-center justify-center shadow-level1 relative z-10">
                <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-mute">1:1</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Square Feed</h4>
            <p class="text-[10px] text-mute font-mono mb-3">1080 x 1080 px • 1:1</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
              The classic format. Perfect for standard posts, grids, and carousels.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Ratio Card 2: 4:5 -->
        <div class="glass-card glass-card-hover rounded-xl p-5 border border-hairline flex flex-col justify-between transition-all duration-200">
          <div>
            <div class="h-24 w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] bg-[radial-gradient(var(--grid-dot)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:8px_8px]"></div>
              <div class="w-10 h-12.5 rounded border border-hairline-strong/60 bg-ink/[0.03] dark:bg-white/[0.03] flex items-center justify-center shadow-level1 relative z-10">
                <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-mute">4:5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Portrait Feed</h4>
            <p class="text-[10px] text-mute font-mono mb-3">1080 x 1350 px • 4:5</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
              Optimized for maximum screen real estate in the Instagram main feed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Ratio Card 3: 9:16 -->
        <div class="glass-card glass-card-hover rounded-xl p-5 border border-hairline flex flex-col justify-between transition-all duration-200">
          <div>
            <div class="h-24 w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] bg-[radial-gradient(var(--grid-dot)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:8px_8px]"></div>
              <div class="w-7 h-14 rounded border border-hairline-strong/60 bg-ink/[0.03] dark:bg-white/[0.03] flex items-center justify-center shadow-level1 relative z-10">
                <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-mute">9:16</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Stories & Reels</h4>
            <p class="text-[10px] text-mute font-mono mb-3">1080 x 1920 px • 9:16</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
              Full-screen vertical layout. Built for Instagram Stories, Reels, and TikTok.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Ratio Card 4: 16:9 -->
        <div class="glass-card glass-card-hover rounded-xl p-5 border border-hairline flex flex-col justify-between transition-all duration-200">
          <div>
            <div class="h-24 w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] bg-[radial-gradient(var(--grid-dot)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:8px_8px]"></div>
              <div class="w-16 h-9 rounded border border-hairline-strong/60 bg-ink/[0.03] dark:bg-white/[0.03] flex items-center justify-center shadow-level1 relative z-10">
                <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-mute">16:9</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Landscape</h4>
            <p class="text-[10px] text-mute font-mono mb-3">1920 x 1080 px • 16:9</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
              Standard widescreen format. Best for YouTube thumbnails and cover photos.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Smart Blur Backgrounds -->
    <div class="border-t border-hairline py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 md:gap-16 items-center">
        <!-- Text -->
        <div class="md:col-span-6 order-2 md:order-1">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft text-[9px] font-mono text-mute mb-4">
            01 / Dynamic Styling
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4 leading-snug">
            Smart Blur Backgrounds
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed mb-4 text-pretty font-normal">
            To <strong class="text-ink font-medium">fit full photo on instagram</strong> without black bars or empty space, our editor dynamically samples colors from your original image to generate a smooth, blurred background.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty font-normal">
            Using the <strong class="text-ink font-medium">add blur background to image online</strong> feature, you can control the blur radius and opacity, creating depth and a modern aesthetic. It works perfectly as a <strong class="text-ink font-medium">blur background for instagram reels</strong> or feed covers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <!-- Visual Component -->
        <div class="md:col-span-6 order-1 md:order-2">
          <div role="img" aria-label="Simulated visualization of an image fitted vertically using blurred background margins" class="relative w-full aspect-video rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center p-6 shadow-level3">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] bg-[radial-gradient(var(--grid-dot)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:8px_8px]"></div>
            <!-- Simulated blurred background canvas -->
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-tr from-violet-500/20 via-indigo-500/25 to-pink-500/20 blur-3xl opacity-60"></div>
            <!-- Centered floating image -->
            <div class="relative w-[30%] aspect-[4/5] rounded-lg border border-white/20 bg-gradient-to-tr from-violet-500 via-indigo-500 to-pink-500 shadow-level4 flex items-center justify-center">
              <div class="text-[9px] font-mono text-white/80 select-none">Original Photo</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Elegant Borders & Margins -->
    <div class="border-t border-hairline py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 md:gap-16 items-center">
        <!-- Visual Component -->
        <div class="md:col-span-6">
          <div role="img" aria-label="Simulated visualization of a widescreen image framed inside a square canvas using white margins" class="relative w-full aspect-video rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center p-6 shadow-level3">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03] bg-[radial-gradient(var(--grid-dot)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:8px_8px]"></div>
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-canvas-soft"></div>
            <!-- Solid margins -->
            <div class="absolute inset-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline flex items-center justify-center shadow-level1">
              <!-- Padded canvas -->
              <div class="w-3/5 aspect-[4/3] rounded bg-gradient-to-tr from-indigo-500 via-cyan-500 to-emerald-400 shadow-level2 flex items-center justify-center border border-black/5">
                <div class="text-[9px] font-mono text-white/80 select-none">Original Photo</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Text -->
        <div class="md:col-span-6">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft text-[9px] font-mono text-mute mb-4">
            02 / Gallery Layout
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4 leading-snug">
            Minimal Borders & Margins
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed mb-4 text-pretty font-normal">
            If you prefer a clean, gallery-like layout, use our <strong class="text-ink font-medium">online photo padding tool</strong> to add custom margins. 
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty font-normal">
            You can <strong class="text-ink font-medium">add white border to instagram photo</strong> uploads or create custom black frames to make your portrait and landscape shots pop. This minimalist style keeps your feed looking consistent and highly professional.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Privacy & Export Cards -->
    <div class="border-t border-hairline py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        
        <!-- Privacy Card -->
        <div class="p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 hover:border-hairline-strong/60 transition-all duration-200 relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between min-h-[240px]">
          <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 p-6 opacity-[0.03] text-ink pointer-events-none">
            <svg class="h-24 w-24" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75m-3-7.036A11.959 11.959 0 013.598 6 11.99 11.99 0 003 9.749c0 5.592 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.31-.21-2.57-.598-3.751h-.152c-3.196 0-6.1-1.248-8.25-3.285z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="relative z-10">
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              Privacy-First Processing
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty font-normal">
              Unlike other online editors, our <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram image resizer online</strong> processes all graphics locally on your device. Since there are no server uploads, your personal data and photos remain completely private.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-[10px] font-mono text-mute relative z-10 select-none">
            <span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            100% Client-Side Processing
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Export Card -->
        <div class="p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft/30 hover:border-hairline-strong/60 transition-all duration-200 relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between min-h-[240px]">
          <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 p-6 opacity-[0.03] text-ink pointer-events-none">
            <svg class="h-24 w-24" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 16.5v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75V16.5M16.5 12L12 16.5m0 0L7.5 12m4.5 4.5V3" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="relative z-10">
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">
              Lossless Quality Export
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed text-pretty font-normal">
              Export high-resolution assets ready for publishing. Easily convert images using our <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram 4:5 resize tool</strong> or prepare a vertical story canvas using the <strong class="text-ink font-medium">instagram story image resizer</strong>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 p-3 rounded-lg bg-canvas-soft/40 border border-hairline/60 text-[10px] text-mute leading-relaxed relative z-10">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Optimization:</span> Select JPEG to optimize file size, or choose PNG if your photo contains fine text details or watermarks.
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Decorative Glow -->
  <div class="absolute top-1/2 left-0 z-0 pointer-events-none opacity-20 -translate-y-1/2 -translate-x-1/3">
    <div class="w-[500px] h-[500px] rounded-full blur-[150px] bg-gradient-to-tr from-violet/20 to-indigo/25"></div>
  </div>
</section>
